Let me just do it properly:

```c
static const char *path_basename(const char *path) {
    size_t len = strlen(path);
    // Remove trailing slashes
    while (len > 1 && path[len-1] == '/') len--;
    // Now find the last '/' in path[0..len)
    const char *last_slash = NULL;
    for (const char *p = path + len; p > path; ) {
        p--;
        if (*p == '/') { last_slash = p; break; }
    }
    if (last_slash) return last_slash + 1;
    return path;
}
```

This handles:
- "foo" → "foo"
- "foo/bar" → "bar"
- "foo/bar/" → "bar"
- "/" → "/" (special case, len becomes 1)
- "" → "" (shouldn't happen)

